PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- All members maintain unanimous consensus that the compounding time of 4:04 AM CST is an algebraic distractor, as Indium-111 decays at the same physical rate regardless of containment.
- The volume required depends strictly on delivering 8.0 mCi at the 8:00 AM Dec 23 administration time against the stock vial calibrated for Dec 26 at 12:00 PM (an effective elapsed interval of 76.0 hours).
- Across standard accepted physical half-life values for Indium-111 (67.2 to 67.44 hours), the calculated volume stably converges between 3.65 mL and 3.66 mL (approximately 3.7 mL).
- Moving forward, continue supporting the consensus range of 3.65 mL to 3.66 mL.
}

